# `yarn prettier` uses this file as its ignore list, not .gitignore, so anything
# gitignored but not listed here makes `yarn test:other` fail on a machine that
# has simply run the tooling. /test-results and /playwright-report are output of
# this repo's own `yarn test:visual`; .claude and .infigraph are the local
# code-intelligence index — .gitnexus is its successor and is listed below,
# which it was not for eight days. None of them is source, and none is
# committed.
/test-results
/playwright-report
/blob-report
.claude
.infigraph

# Gitignored, but prettier reads THIS file rather than .gitignore, so anything
# ignored by git has to be listed here too or `yarn test:other` fails on a file
# that is not part of the repository.
#
# `.superpowers/` is subagent scratch. The rest are the working brief and the
# process material behind it: still on disk for whoever works in this checkout,
# no longer published, and no longer anybody's job to keep formatted.
.superpowers/
CLAUDE.md
docs/superpowers/
docs/agents/
.github/copilot-instructions.md

# Same trap, sprung again on 2026-08-26: `yarn test:other` had been red since
# 2026-08-18 and nobody saw it, because nobody runs a gate that is not in CI.
# `graphify-out/` is the knowledge graph `/graphify` writes; AGENTS.md is the
# generated working brief. Both are gitignored, neither is source.
graphify-out/
AGENTS.md
.gitnexus/
.obsidian/

# One deployment's own notes: its URL, its administrator, which of its
# protections are off. `.gitignore` covers `*.local.md` so those facts never
# reach a repository other people clone — but prettier reads THIS file, and a
# note somebody wrote by hand is not source anybody should have to format.
# Without this line `yarn test:other` fails the moment an operator writes one,
# which teaches them that the gate is noise.
*.local.md
